WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.060
- [Mark] All right, Joy.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:05.893
- Yes.

00:00:05.893 --> 00:00:07.018
- [Mark] Joy, where'd you grow up?

00:00:07.018 --> 00:00:07.851
Where are you from, originally?

00:00:07.851 --> 00:00:10.493
- [Joy] I'm from Ohio, Dayton, Ohio.

00:00:10.493 --> 00:00:11.757
- [Mark] And tell me about
your family and your childhood.

00:00:11.757 --> 00:00:13.840
You had both your parents
when you were a kid?

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.870
- [Joy] Yeah. Well, I started out

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.970
livin' with my grandmother,

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.290
who I thought was my mom, 'til she died.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.220
Then I started livin' with my mom,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.703
who I thought was my cousin.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:29.370
From then, 4 to 17, I was
molested on a daily basis,

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:33.310
three family members. A
pastor. I got married.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.290
- [Mark] Pastor as well?

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:39.290
- Yeah. I got married, had
two children by a married man.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:46.463
That ended. Then I got married again.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:52.350
This was a real thug type of
guy. Real penitentiary type.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.870
And I thought he was a big dope dealer,

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.180
and I was fascinated
with just, his lifestyle.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.947
But then I found out, he
had a big habit, to crack.

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:08.343
And he had relapsed and he
didn't tell me none of that.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:12.873
So, found out he was doin' all
kinda stuff to get his dope.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:17.663
But he was on the down
low, that was the ultimate.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.640
- [Mark] So he was dating guys as well,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.920
or having sex with guys.
- To get money. Big money.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.130
- [Mark] Oh, he was getting paid for it?

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.680
- Oh yeah.
- [Mark] All right.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.690
- So, I asked him for my money back,

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.910
'cause I was the type of woman,

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.730
any money that came to me workin',

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.593
social security, or whatever,
I would give to my man.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:45.590
And I wanted to leave. He
didn't want me to leave,

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:48.020
he wanted to tell the
truth, but I have found out,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.890
so I didn't wanna know the truth,

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.960
whatever he called the truth.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.580
And so, he gave me his
dope. He took dope out,

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.973
hit the dope, made a pipe, just amazed me,

00:02:02.153 --> 00:02:04.373
and offered it to me, and just was stuck.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:08.440
And I got upset, took it,
and calmed myself on it.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.520
Just smoke it, smoke it up.
(breathing quickly)

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.950
That way he ain't got no dope left,

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.700
he gon' have no money, you know, anything.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.640
Little did I know, two weeks later,

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.323
I was chasing the same shit.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.880
And it's been since 2000
that I been struggling.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.803
I'm at my lowest today.

00:02:33.399 --> 00:02:35.316
I'm literally homeless.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.970
And I'm doing any and
everything to survive.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.163
That's my story.

00:02:46.163 --> 00:02:48.080
- [Mark] What kinda stuff
do you have to go through

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.150
just to make money?

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:54.150
- Steal. Sell my body.
Negotiate my morals.

00:03:03.364 --> 00:03:05.110
And it's not always for dope.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.453
Sometimes it's to eat,

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.350
sometimes it's to have
a roof over my head,

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.093
even if it's just a tent.

00:03:14.053 --> 00:03:17.354
(traffic whirring in background)

00:03:17.354 --> 00:03:21.643
It don't just be for dope.

00:03:21.643 --> 00:03:24.662
It don't just be for dope.

00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:26.653
It be for everything.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.333
I'm livin' to use, and I'm usin' to live.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.631
That's my story.

00:03:33.631 --> 00:03:35.090
- [Mark] And do you have children?

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.390
- It's two. They're grown.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.230
- [Mark] You have the
two kids that you had

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.940
with the married man?
- Yeah.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.460
- [Mark] You raised them?

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:45.410
- No, my daughter stayed with my sister,

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.510
up until the addictions started happenin'.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.840
But my son was a ride or die 'til the end.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:53.673
- [Mark] He what?

00:03:53.673 --> 00:03:55.773
- My son was with me 'til the very end.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:58.320
He had to let me go,

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.350
'cause I kept gettin' us in predicaments

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:03.303
where we had to move,
had to move, had to move.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:08.420
And at one point, I didn't
find a place soon enough,

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.440
so he needed to stay with my parents,

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:14.780
and the anger started and since then-

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.353
- [Mark] Had you ever used
drugs before your husband?

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:21.380
It was just that one time got you hooked?

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:26.380
- I was 37 years old when I
started, when that happened.

00:04:28.357 --> 00:04:30.493
- [Mark] And you haven't
been able to stop since?

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.770
- I had two or three
years, couple of times.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.630
But it's what I choose.
- [Mark] You relapse?

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:48.376
- It's what I choose.

00:04:48.376 --> 00:04:49.209
- [Mark] What do you think
people don't understand

00:04:49.209 --> 00:04:52.620
about the power of crack or addiction?

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:57.620
- That it's really a disease,
it's really a disease.

00:04:57.737 --> 00:04:59.447
- [Mark] It's not a
decision you're making?

00:04:59.447 --> 00:05:00.727
- No. Not anymore.

00:05:00.727 --> 00:05:01.560
- [Mark] It's not a bad decision-

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:02.900
- You start off makin' a decision.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.370
- [Mark] Yeah. The first
time is maybe a decision,

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:07.246
but after that, it
becomes beyond your power.

00:05:07.246 --> 00:05:10.950
- You don't have more.
You don't have a decision.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:14.450
There are times when I can go, shoot,

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:17.210
maybe two or three months,

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:20.960
and I'm cool, I'm cool.
And all of a sudden,

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:25.250
I can get a urge that's
beyond the phenomenon,

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:29.360
or craving, that obsession
that, I mean, it's beyond it.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.910
It's beyond it, it's
like, I gotta do anything.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.523
So I've been going to mental
hospitals too, because,

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.600
I get to thinkin' about suicide,

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:43.267
'cause I'm tired of livin'
dirty, and nasty, and secretive.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.857
I'm tired of bein'
laughed at, and put down.

00:05:51.797 --> 00:05:54.680
(hands rubbing)

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.260
- [Mark] Do you have any friends?

00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:00.730
- I just met one that I had
long time ago, in Compton.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:05.123
He's really old, and I didn't
know where he had went,

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:09.960
and I just seen him, it's
been maybe three years now.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.870
He said he got an apartment
through the VA in Radier.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:17.160
So, he's offered me to
take a shower and eat,

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:21.087
and lay down and get some
rest. (laughs softly)

00:06:21.087 --> 00:06:24.180
So that's who I was talkin' to
when I was cross the street.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:27.320
- [Mark] Where do you sleep?
Where'd you sleep last night?

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.900
- Last night at a church.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:33.800
I go to churches that is pretty
lit up and have security,

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.960
'cause they are huge.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:40.803
The one where Farrah Fawcett
funeral was, the real big one.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.423
But it's scary anywhere.

00:06:46.309 --> 00:06:49.300
- [Mark] What kinda bad stuff
has happened to you out here?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:53.447
- The robbin', just having
you do the sexual acts,

00:06:56.340 --> 00:07:00.230
and not payin' you the money,
throwing you out of a car.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.353
Throwing you out of a car. Lied on.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.050
- [Mark] Then after a few weeks of this,

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:14.570
the shame becomes-
- Unbearable.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:16.730
- [Mark] Another thing
that makes you use more.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:19.443
- Yep. And the guilt.
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:07:21.234 --> 00:07:24.997
Do you have hope of
getting out, permanently?

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:31.100
- I feel like, if there is
a way, then it'll happen.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.680
But I'm not tryna make it happen no more.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.610
Because I can't do, thank you,

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:44.063
I can't do for me, what I
feel like only God can do.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:49.520
And I feel like God is
sayin', until I can say no,

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:52.773
this is the decision I gotta
make, and I gotta stick to it.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:57.213
Only he can keep me, but
I gotta wanna be kept.

00:07:58.467 --> 00:07:59.603
And I'm not there yet.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:04.900
- [Mark] What's the most important lesson

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:06.723
you think you've learned in your life?

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:11.943
- Don't judge people.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.673
'Cause I called my
husband a crack head hoe,

00:08:19.684 --> 00:08:22.557
and that's what I became.
And now I understand.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.183
- [Mark] Would you describe
yourself as depressed?

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:33.535
- [Joy] Yeah, I'm manic depressed.

00:08:33.535 --> 00:08:35.740
'Cause I'm mad, 'cause I understand,

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.610
so I don't have anymore
excuses. (laughs softly)

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:42.500
So that makes me angry.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:46.603
So when I do drugs, I don't feel anything.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:51.350
I know it, 'cause our
problems don't go no where,

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:54.433
they don't be waitin' on us.
They be right in the head.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.427
- [Mark] And you were good friends with

00:09:01.427 --> 00:09:03.220
one of my favorite-
- [Joy] Yeah. (laughs)

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:04.390
- [Mark] People I've interviewed,

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:05.890
- [Joy] Right.
- [Mark] Alicia.

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.710
- [Joy] Yeah.
- [Mark] Did you guys

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:10.070
used to talk about your addiction?

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:13.710
- [Joy] Yeah, we lived in the
same room in the Weingart,

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:17.967
and it's like, people just
allowin' things to happen.

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:23.117
'Cause they smokin' and
everything in the Weingart,

00:09:23.117 --> 00:09:25.340
and the caseworkers, and so forth, know.

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:27.440
- [Mark] But for a woman
who's addicted to crack,

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:31.200
you end up, (sighs deeply)
you're at the mercy

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.930
of these men down here that will just

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.450
do everything and anything, right?

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:36.283
- [Joy] And anything.

00:09:36.283 --> 00:09:37.150
- [Mark] They don't care about age,

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:38.640
they don't care about pregnancies,

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.441
they don't care about
black eyes or broken bones.

00:09:41.441 --> 00:09:43.765
- [Joy] And most them are down, though.

00:09:43.765 --> 00:09:45.000
- [Mark] Yeah.
- [Joy] Most of 'em.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.100
And they takin' out stuff on women,

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.175
because they're not wanted,

00:09:51.175 --> 00:09:52.810
and they feel like, we're stupid,

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:57.410
because if we knew how
to work this, we would.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:02.410
But, no. 'Cause what you're
doin', is what we're doing.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:06.880
It's just a different way.
And that's the problem,

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:11.880
because they feeling raped
and robbed of they souls.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.010
Lotta them were takin' advantage of.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:25.373
The rage, the vengeance,
is on the wrong people.

00:10:31.434 --> 00:10:32.930
A lotta times you get treated bad,

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:37.137
because they can see in your
eyes that you can see 'em,

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:39.443
behind the veil.

00:10:40.472 --> 00:10:42.030
- [Mark] What was the
best part of your life?

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.190
Best time of your life?

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:46.120
- When I was about seven,

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.423
in the second grade when we moved here,

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:54.063
before the molestin'
started here, in California.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:59.900
I won a contest for how you
keep your keys safe. (chuckles)

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:02.830
So they gave this great big old trophy,

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.713
that was probably big as
me, in the shape of a key.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:11.160
My teacher cared, so I
wanted to be a teacher.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:17.770
- [Mark] Do you think that
the sexual abuse you had

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:21.150
from those four different
people, when you were very young,

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:24.010
may have changed the course of your life?

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:27.290
- Oh yeah. Because my mom and people knew,

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.610
and it was like they were allowin' us

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:31.133
to be just passed around.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:33.290
- [Mark] Your parents knew?

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:38.220
- My mom. But then I found
out my mom was going through

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:40.790
a lot of incest and had been raped a lot,

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:45.790
and had a lot of illegal
abortions, by her uncles.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.680
And she told me didn't
know how to help me,

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:51.630
she learned how to black it
out, she thought I would. Yeah.

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:59.514
- [Mark] If you could of changed
one thing about your life,

00:11:59.514 --> 00:12:03.000
what would you of-
- What would I change?

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.260
- [Mark] What would you change?

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:09.230
- My choice.
- [Mark] To use?

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:10.864
- Yep.
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:12:10.864 --> 00:12:14.000
(Joy sobs softly)

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:14.833
- [Mark] All right, Joy.

00:12:14.833 --> 00:12:16.323
Well thank you for coming
in and talking with me

00:12:16.323 --> 00:12:17.293
- Thank you.

00:12:17.293 --> 00:12:18.700
- [Mark] And good luck getting clean.

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:21.083
I hope you turn the corner on this.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:24.800
One day when you're done, you'll be done,

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:27.383
and you just turn your back and move on.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:31.590
- Thank you, Mark. (laughs softly)

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:36.533
My tears are drying up.
Almost can't even cry no more.

00:12:36.533 --> 00:12:40.153
I have moments, I might
get 'em to come back,

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:45.060
but can't even cry no more, that's it.

00:12:46.071 --> 00:12:48.571
(sobs softly)

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:52.080
- [Mark] Let me get you
a room tonight, at least.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.020
- What? (laughs softly)

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.029
- [Mark] Yeah, I'll
get you a room tonight.

00:12:55.029 --> 00:12:56.234
- Oh my God.

00:12:56.234 --> 00:12:57.067
- [Mark] You think after that I'm gonna

00:12:57.067 --> 00:12:58.117
let you sleep on the street?

00:12:59.576 --> 00:13:02.409
I can't do that.
- Wow. Thank you.

00:13:05.157 --> 00:13:08.647
(mic clattering)

00:13:08.647 --> 00:13:10.356
- [Mark] And a friend of Alicia's.

00:13:10.356 --> 00:13:11.189
(Joy laughing)

00:13:11.189 --> 00:13:12.777
How could I not take care of you?

00:13:13.955 --> 00:13:15.096
- Oh my God.

00:13:15.096 --> 00:13:16.051
- [Mark] Does that get you a room tonight?

00:13:16.051 --> 00:13:19.301
- Oh my God. Yes, oh my God. Thank you.

00:13:22.186 --> 00:13:24.519
Thank you, thank you, Jesus.

00:13:26.151 --> 00:13:28.913
You both remind me of her. (laughs softly)

00:13:28.913 --> 00:13:31.340
Y'all are some Daisy Duke's
with some boots. (laughs)

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:33.628
- [Mark] No, Alicia was great (indistinct)

00:13:33.628 --> 00:13:35.799
- [Joy] Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:13:35.799 --> 00:13:36.632
- [Mark] All right, then.

00:13:36.632 --> 00:13:39.107
- [Joy] You have a great day.
- [Mark] You too.

00:13:39.107 --> 00:13:39.940
Thank you, stop crying.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:41.290
- [Joy] Bye.
- [Mark] Bye.

